# Android build & emulator deploy

Whenever you change Android app code or Gradle config under `app/`:

1. Run `.\gradlew :app:assembleDebug` before finishing the turn.
2. The build copies the APK to `outputs/WordBuddy-debug.apk` automatically.
3. Install and launch on the connected emulator (default `emulator-5554`):
   - `adb -s emulator-5554 install -r outputs/WordBuddy-debug.apk`
   - `adb -s emulator-5554 shell monkey -p com.hotgis.wordbuddy -c android.intent.category.LAUNCHER 1`
4. If no emulator is connected, report that briefly; do not skip the build.

Do not skip the build/deploy cycle after substantive Android UI/logic changes unless the user explicitly opts out for that turn.
